# Production build config. Vite inlines these at build time, so a shipped app
# binary is permanently pinned to whatever host was set here when it was built —
# changing the backend URL later means a rebuild and, for the native apps, a
# store resubmission. Set this before `npm run sync`.
#
# This must be a domain Railway serves **publicly** — the custom domain below, or
# the generated `*.up.railway.app` one (Settings → Networking → Public
# Networking). A `*.railway.internal` hostname resolves only inside the Railway
# project, and the clients here are browsers and phones outside it — it would
# fail exactly like a dead host, only less obviously.
#
# Pinned to the custom domain rather than the generated one on purpose: a shipped
# binary cannot be repointed, so the host it names has to be one that outlives
# the Railway service behind it.
#
# https/wss are mandatory for the native apps: iOS App Transport Security and
# Android's cleartextTrafficPermitted=false both block plain http/ws, even on a
# LAN. See ../backend/DEPLOY.md.
VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://api.watchlondonmove.maybeitssoftware.co.uk
VITE_SOCKET_URL=https://api.watchlondonmove.maybeitssoftware.co.uk
VITE_INTERPOLATION_MS=12000
VITE_MAP_STYLE=https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron
